---
description: Clean, reusable code standards. No slop.
alwaysApply: true
---

- Write the minimum code that solves the task. No speculative features, unused params, or "just in case" abstractions.
- Single responsibility: one function does one thing; keep functions under ~40 lines and files focused.
- DRY: extract shared logic (auth guard, error handler, validation, API response helpers) into src/lib and reuse it. Search for an existing helper before writing a new one.
- Strict TypeScript: no `any`, no non-null `!` hacks; infer types from Zod schemas and Drizzle tables.
- Clear names over comments. Comment only the _why_, never restate the code. No banner comments, no emojis, no TODO filler.
- No dead code, console.logs, commented-out blocks, or placeholder/mock data left behind.
- Handle errors once, centrally: throw typed AppError(code, status, message); route handlers use one shared wrapper to format responses.
- Never swallow errors with empty catch blocks.
- Config and secrets only via a validated env module (src/lib/env.ts with Zod); never read process.env elsewhere.
- Don't add a dependency if a few lines or an existing package does the job.
- Before finishing: run lint, typecheck and tests; re-read the diff and delete anything not needed.
- If a request is unclear, ask instead of guessing.
